WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.370
Spider-Man is speaking out at D23 Expo 2019.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.839
Things haven't been easy lately for actor
Tom Holland.

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:10.500
He's had one of the worst weeks an actor could
have after the unthinkable happened: news

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.540
broke that Disney and Sony failed to renegotiate
their 2015 deal.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.130
That landmark agreement allowed Holland's
Sony-owned Spider-Man to appear in movies

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:22.419
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe, earning
money for Sony while Marvel maintained creative

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:23.419
input.

00:00:23.419 --> 00:00:27.970
If a new deal really isn't being negotiated,
it means that Spider-Man is leaving the MCU.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.759
In other words, Holland's world got flipped
upside down.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:35.329
His future with both Marvel Studios and Sony
Pictures was called into question, and his

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:39.399
millions of adoring fans wondered why he wasn't
speaking out about the situation.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:43.310
One would imagine that Holland, a longtime
Spider-Man fan, would be devastated over the

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:46.739
Disney-Sony divorce - and apparently, they'd
be mostly right.

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:51.719
Holland finally broke his silence about the
studio split during D23 Expo on Saturday,

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:53.020
August 24.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:57.579
Taking the stage to promote his upcoming movie
Onward, a Pixar animated flick also featuring

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:01.440
Marvel favorite Chris Pratt, Holland admitted
that he's been having a rough time since the

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.360
news dropped, and he's trying to focus on
what matters most.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.650
Though Holland didn't say much about the corporate
spat, the message he did deliver to his fans

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:09.650
was an emotional one:

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:13.680
"It's been a crazy week, but I want you to
know I am grateful from the bottom of my heart,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.960
and I love you 3,000."

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.360
"3000, that's crazy.”

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.800
The 23-year-old actor's candid admission is
both refreshing and heartbreaking, and his

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.730
mention that he's genuinely thankful for his
fans and for the opportunity to play Spider-Man

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.930
over the years is enough to make anyone shed
a tear or two.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.490
After the presentation at D23, Holland spoke
with Entertainment Weekly about leaving the

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:41.130
MCU, promising that he'll keep stepping into
the Spidey suit for as long as he can and

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.720
continue making the franchise as great as
it can be.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:44.799
He told the magazine,

00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:46.750
"Basically, we've made five great movies.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.299
It's been five amazing years.

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:49.640
I've had the time of my life.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.450
Who knows what the future holds?

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:54.719
But all I know is that I'm going to continue
playing Spider-Man and having the time of

00:01:54.719 --> 00:01:55.719
my life.

00:01:55.719 --> 00:01:58.200
It's going to be so fun, however we choose
to do it."

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.200
He added optimistically,

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.469
"The future for Spider-Man will be different,
but it will be equally as awesome and amazing,

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:05.820
and we'll find new ways to make it even cooler."

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:10.259
Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige, who
produced both Homecoming and Far From Home,

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:13.800
also addressed the situation, echoing Holland
with his own optimistic viewpoint.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.800
He said,

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.340
"[What] I'm feeling about Spider-Man [is]
gratitude and joy.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.790
We got to make five films within the MCU with
Spider-Man: two standalone films and three

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.050
with the Avengers.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.130
It was a dream that I never thought would
happen.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.760
It was never meant to last forever.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.510
We knew there was a finite amount of time
that we'd be able to do this, and we told

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.930
the story we wanted to tell, and I'll always
be thankful for that."

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.540
Yeah, but tell that to Far From Home's cliffhanger
ending.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.500
In a perfect world, Holland would have never
needed to address the Disney-Sony breakup

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.870
because it never would have happened.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.810
If all had gone the way everyone truly wanted
it to go, the two companies would have been

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.010
able to reach an agreement to keep Spider-Man
in the MCU.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:52.870
Far From Home served as the conclusion for
Marvel's Phase 3, and considering how much

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:57.500
emphasis the movie placed on Spider-Man as
a successor to Tony Stark, many were pondering

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.620
the character's place in the upcoming Phase
4 and beyond.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.951
A third Spider-Man movie continuing Peter
Parker's story felt inevitable, but now that

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:09.080
the character's connections to the MCU have
apparently been severed, no one knows what

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.519
that movie is going to look like.

00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:14.670
Before the news broke, it felt like Holland's
Spider-Man was going to avoid the same fate

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.770
as Andrew Garfield's iteration of the character,
and would get to complete his trilogy and

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:19.770
then some.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.450
But it looks those assumptions were wrong.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:25.670
There's no telling what will happen for Holland's
Spider-Man next, but one thing's for sure:

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.040
no matter what, fans will be telling the actor
that they love him 3,000 for years to come.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.240
"What am I even tripping for?

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:35.800
Everything's going to work out exactly the
way it's supposed to."

